&gt;

&gt; For countries:

&gt;

&gt; VV -&gt; gugde'V'V

&gt; VC -&gt; gugde'VCu

&gt; CV -&gt; gugdeCu'V

&gt; CC -&gt; gugdeCuCu

&gt;

&gt; Codes with "h", "q", "w", "y" use "xe", "ke", "ve", "je" instead of

&gt; "xu", "ku", "vu", "ju".

&gt;

&gt; For languages:

&gt;

&gt; VVV -&gt; bangV'V'V

&gt; VVC -&gt; bangV'V'Cu

&gt; VCV -&gt; bangVCu'V

&gt; VCC -&gt; bangVCuCu

&gt;

&gt; CVV -&gt; banCu'V'V

&gt; CVC -&gt; banCu'VCu

&gt; CCV -&gt; banCuCu'V

&gt; CCC -&gt; banCuCuCu

&gt;

&gt; special case: codes that start with "n" or "g":

&gt;

&gt; (n|g)VV -&gt; baur(n|g)u'V'V

&gt; (n|g)VC -&gt; baur(n|g)u'VCu

&gt; (n|g)CV -&gt; baur(n|g)uCu'V

&gt; (n|g)CC -&gt; baur(n|g)uCuCu

&gt;

&gt; mu'o mi'e xorxes



